Log out of an observe server.

  Revokes the user API key that `nexora login` saved for the server and deletes
  it from ~/.nexora/credentials. If the server cannot be reached, the local copy
  is still deleted and the key expires on its own.


  Over plain http:// to another machine the key or password could be read on
  the way, so the command refuses unless you pass --allow-insecure-http. Use an
  https:// URL (for example behind a TLS proxy) instead. Localhost is fine.
  Examples
  ────────
    nexora logout
    nexora logout --server https://nexora.internal:9464
